# EPDS — Organisms & Pages Catalog

## Global Chrome

### `GlobalHeader` — `src/components/GlobalHeader/`
- **Figma**: Site header — full-width, responsive (DT/TB/MB via CSS media queries)
- **Props**: `variant?: 'global' | 'global-search' | 'homepage' | 'homepage-search' | 'purchase'` (default `'global'`), `guest?: boolean` (default `false`), `zipCode?: string`, `phoneNumber?: string`, `searchPlaceholder?: string`, `logoHref?: string`, `logoUrl?: string`, `logoLightUrl?: string`, `brandName?: string` (default `'EchoPark Automotive'`), `navLinks?: NavLink[]`
- **Type export**: `NavLink` — `{ label: string, href?: string, dropdown?: boolean }`
- **Emits**: `search`, `menu-click`, `location-click`, `favorites-click`, `profile-click`, `sign-in-click`, `more-click`
- **Brand configuration**: All brand-specific content (logo, brand name, nav links) is prop-driven. Pass Sonic values via props — no component changes needed.
- **Stories**: EP variants (global, global-search, homepage, homepage-search, purchase) + Sonic variants (global, global-guest, global-search, purchase)
- **Storybook `title`**: `Organisms/GlobalHeader`

### `GlobalFooter` — `src/components/GlobalFooter/`
- **Figma**: Site footer — full-width, responsive (DT/TB/MB via CSS container queries)
- **Props**: `phoneNumber?: string`, `logoHref?: string`, `logoUrl?: string`, `brandName?: string` (default `'EchoPark Automotive'`), `linkColumns?: FooterLinkColumn[]`, `socialLinks?: SocialLink[]`, `trustBadges?: TrustBadge[]`, `legalLinks?: LegalLink[]`, `copyrightText?: string`
- **Type exports**:
  - `FooterLinkColumn` — `{ heading: string, links: { label: string, href: string }[] }`
  - `SocialLink` — `{ platform: string, href: string, ariaLabel: string }` (icon resolved from built-in platform→SVG map; supported platforms: `facebook`, `x`, `youtube`, `instagram`, `tiktok`)
  - `TrustBadge` — `{ src: string, alt: string, height?: number }`
  - `LegalLink` — `{ label: string, href: string }`
- **Brand configuration**: All content is prop-driven with EchoPark defaults. Pass `trustBadges: []` to hide badges entirely.
- **Stories**: EP viewports (Desktop, Tablet, Mobile, AllViewports) + Sonic variants (Desktop, Mobile, AllViewports)
- **Storybook `title`**: `Organisms/GlobalFooter`

### Brand configuration pattern (GlobalHeader + GlobalFooter)
Both site chrome components follow the same pattern: **EchoPark content is the default; other brands override via props.**
- **Colours** adapt automatically via the semantic token / primitives swap (e.g. `--color-action-primary` becomes red for Sonic).
- **Content** (logos, links, badges, phone numbers) is passed as structured props.
- **Storybook** stories for each brand demonstrate the configuration; use the Brand toolbar toggle to preview colour theming.

## Sonic Nav Bar

### `SonicNavBar` — `src/components/SonicNavBar/`
- **Figma**: "Frame 2492" (node `7639:20938`) — single nav frame with five Property 1 variants. **Default** (desktop bar, 1440×72), **Variant 2** (mobile bar, 375×64), **Variant 3** (desktop with mega-menu open, 1440×412), **Variant 4** (mobile drawer with parent list, 375×552), **Variant 5** (mobile drawer drilled into a parent submenu, 375×952).
- **Role**: Sonic-style global navigation organism. Composes every nav atom in the system: `NavItem` (desktop primary nav + dropdown triggers), `NavItemMobile` (mobile drawer parent rows), `NavItemSubmenu` (drilled submenu leaf links), `MenuToggle` (hamburger / close), `NavIconButton` (favourites + profile), `BaseButton` (primary CTA), `Divider` (mobile drilled-submenu separator).
- **Props**: `navItems: NavBarItem[]` (**required**), `logoUrl?: string` (default Sonic SA-FullColor logo), `logoHref?: string` (default `'/'`), `brandName?: string` (default `'Sonic Automotive'`), `ctaLabel?: string` (default `'Join the Sonic Circuit'`), `ctaHref?: string`, `favoritesHref?: string` (default `'/favorites'`), `profileHref?: string` (default `'/account'`), `favoritesSelected?: boolean`, `profileSelected?: boolean`, `forceMobile?: boolean` (Storybook escape hatch), `sticky?: boolean` (default `true`)
- **Type exports**:
  - `NavBarLink` — `{ label: string, href?: string }`
  - `NavBarSection` — `{ heading: string, links: NavBarLink[] }`
  - `NavBarItem` — `{ key: string, label: string, href?: string, dropdown?: NavBarSection[] }`. When `dropdown` is omitted the item is a direct link. When supplied, the item becomes a desktop dropdown trigger and a drilled-mobile parent row.
- **Emits**: `cta-click`, `favorites-click`, `profile-click`, `submenu-link-click: [{ item, link, event }]`, `nav-item-click: [{ item, event }]`
- **Layout** (toolbar):
  - **Desktop** (≥ 1440 px / full Figma spec): 72 px height, 80 px horizontal padding. Logo (104 × 41 px) + horizontal nav (49 px gap) + favourites/profile + primary CTA.
  - **Mid-range desktop progressive tightening** (1024–1439 px): tightens spacing in three steps:
    - **1280–1439 px**: page gutter 80 → 32 px, nav gap 49 → 32 px, bar inter-cluster gap 32 → 24 px
    - **1024–1279 px**: nav gap 32 → 24 px, utility cluster + icons gap 24 → 16 px
    - **1024–1199 px**: hide the desktop CTA so the icons sit flush against the nav. The CTA still renders inside the mobile drawer at <1024.
  - **Mobile** (< 1024 px or `forceMobile`): 64 px height, 24 px horizontal padding. Logo (94 × 37 px) + favourites/profile + `MenuToggle`.
- **Mega-menu** (Variant 3 — desktop only):
  - Opens flush below the toolbar with `border-top: 1px solid var(--color-nav-active-indicator)` (Sonic dark red `#D9320D`, EchoPark green).
  - 80 px / 40 px padding. Section columns laid out with `gap: 119px`. Second section auto-wraps into a 2-column grid.
  - Section heading: 18 px Bold; links: 16 px Regular; focus ring: 3 px `--color-nav-focus-ring` outline.
  - Only one dropdown open at a time. Click outside / press `Escape` to close.
- **Mobile drawer** (Variant 4 + 5):
  - Slides in below the 64 px bar with the same brand-coloured `border-top`. Body scroll locks while open.
  - **Parent list (Variant 4)**: vertical stack of `NavItemMobile` rows (40 px gap). CTA button pinned to the bottom.
  - **Drilled submenu (Variant 5)**: back-arrow header on top, then each section as a labelled block, separated by `Divider color="light"`.
- **Keyboard**: `Escape` collapses one level at a time — drilled submenu → parent drawer → desktop dropdown.
- **Brand awareness**: Component itself is brand-agnostic. CTA themes red on Sonic / green on EchoPark via `BaseButton variant="primary"`. Mega-menu / drawer top border reads from `--color-nav-active-indicator` (Sonic `#D9320D`, EchoPark `var(--color-base-primary-50)`).
- **Stories** (`Organisms/SonicNavBar`): `Default` (desktop bar with placeholder body), `Variant 2 — mobile bar`, `Variant 3 — desktop mega-menu open`, `Variant 4 — mobile drawer parent list`, `Variant 5 — mobile drilled submenu`, `Interactive` (fully interactive sandbox)
- **Token additions**: `--color-nav-active-indicator` added to **both** `primitives/echopark.css` and `primitives/sonic.css`. EchoPark maps it to `var(--color-base-primary-50)`; Sonic maps it to `var(--color-btn-primary-surface-hover)` (`#D9320D`).
- **Storybook `title`**: `Organisms/SonicNavBar`

## Sonic Circuit Section

### `SonicCircuit` — `src/components/SonicCircuit/`
- **Figma**: "The Sonic Circuit" — desktop node `7680:16688`, mobile node `7680:16721`. Full-bleed dark-navy panel pitching the Sonic Circuit rewards membership.
- **Role**: Reusable "membership benefits" organism. Composes a stack of `SonicCircuitBenefit` atoms between a centered title block and a primary `BaseButton` CTA. Every label and the benefit list is prop-driven.
- **Props**: `title?: string` (default `'The Sonic Circuit'`), `subtitle?: string` (default `'One membership across every Sonic brand nationwide.'`), `benefits: SonicCircuitBenefitItem[]` (**required** — designed for 3–4 items per Figma), `ctaLabel?: string` (default `'Join the Circuit'`), `ctaHref?: string`, `ariaLabel?: string`
- **Type export**: `SonicCircuitBenefitItem` — `{ id: string; iconSvg: string; caption: string }`. `iconSvg` is the raw SVG markup (import with `?raw`).
- **Emits**: `cta-click: [event: MouseEvent]`
- **Composes**: `SonicCircuitBenefit` (one per item in `benefits`) + `BaseButton variant="primary" size="md"` for the CTA.
- **Layout**: Full-bleed `<section>` with a fixed `#25303d` navy background. Inner content rail is `max-width: 1440px` with `padding: 80px`. Outer flex column with `gap: 68px` between heading / benefits / CTA. Heading is a 564 px centered column (title 42 / 54 / -1.2; subtitle 24 / 1.3 / -0.264). Benefits row is a `<ul role="list">` flex row with `gap: 47px` and `justify-content: center`. CTA wrapped at `width: 175px` (Figma spec).
- **Responsive**:
  - **Desktop (≥1024)** — 80 px section padding, 4-up benefits row, 68 px gap
  - **Tablet (≤1023)** — Section padding `64px 32px`; outer gap 56 px; benefits row gets `flex-wrap: wrap` with `gap: 47px 32px`
  - **Mobile (<600)** — Section padding `40px 24px`; outer gap 40 px; title scales to 32 px; benefits stack vertically with 47 px gap
- **Brand awareness**: The CTA uses `BaseButton variant="primary"` so the fill colour automatically themes (Sonic red on Sonic, EchoPark green on EchoPark). The `#25303d` navy is intentionally a section-local literal — promote to a token once a second surface adopts it.
- **Accessibility**: `<section aria-label="…">` landmark (overridable via `ariaLabel`). The benefits row is a `<ul role="list">`. The decorative disks are `aria-hidden="true"`.
- **HomePage integration**: `HomePage.vue` mounts the section directly below `ShopByCategories`. Four Figma-spec benefits seeded using existing system icons reused via `?raw` imports — `Style=Location, Detail=Map-Location`, `Style=Finance, Detail=Payment, Icon=Coin`, `Icon Type=Vehicle Descriptors, Size=Medium, Theme=Steering`, `Icon Type=Vehicle Descriptors, Size=Small, Theme=Medal`.
- **Stories**: `Default`, `Mobile` (375 px viewport), `ThreeBenefits`, `TwoBenefits`, `CustomCopy`
- **Storybook `title`**: `Organisms/SonicCircuit`

