## Brand Portfolio

### `BrandPortfolio` — `src/components/BrandPortfolio/`
- **Figma**: "Brand Portfolio" frame — first sub-frame shows all four cards in default state; the next four sub-frames show one of Sonic Automotive / EchoPark / Tactical Fleet / Powersports expanded.
- **Role**: Organism that composes 4 (configurable to N) `BrandShowcaseCard` molecules into a horizontal row with **exactly-one** selection state. Clicking a collapsed card animates the row so the new card grows to 384 px while the other three flex equally to fill the remaining width.
- **Props**:
  - `brands: BrandShowcaseEntry[]` (**required**) — array of card configs; each entry mirrors `BrandShowcaseCard`'s prop surface plus a stable `key` and an optional `ctaLabel` (set to `undefined` to suppress the molecule's default single-CTA when a `#cta-<key>` slot is provided instead)
  - `modelValue?: string | null` (v-model) — currently selected card's `key`. Pass `null` to render the "all collapsed" Figma frame.
  - `selectFirstByDefault?: boolean` (default `true`) — when `modelValue` is `undefined` at mount, initialise selection to `brands[0].key`. Set to `false` (and pass `:modelValue="null"`) for the "Default" / "all collapsed" story.
- **Emits**:
  - `update:modelValue: [string | null]`
  - `select: [key: string]`
  - `cta-click: [{ key: string, event: MouseEvent }]`
- **Slots** (per-brand, dynamic by `brand.key`):
  - `#content-<key>` — replaces `BrandShowcaseCard`'s `#selected-content` slot for the specified brand.
  - `#cta-<key>` (scope: `{ onCtaClick: (event: MouseEvent) => void }`) — replaces `BrandShowcaseCard`'s `#cta` override slot. EchoPark uses this to render a primary + secondary `BaseButton` pair side-by-side.
- **Layout**:
  - **Desktop (≥ 600 px)**: row capped at `max-width: 1286px`, `margin: 0 auto`, no gap between cards. Selected slot is `flex: 0 0 384px`; collapsed slots are `flex: 1 1 0; max-width: 322px`. The molecule's `--bsc-width-collapsed` / `--bsc-width-selected` CSS vars are overridden to `100%`.
  - **Mobile (≤ 599 px)**: row stacks vertically; cards keep their 322 / 384 px widths and centre horizontally. Tap-to-expand still works the same as desktop.
- **Animation**: the row's flex-basis transitions sync with the molecule's `width` transition (both `0.3s ease`)
- **Stories** (`Organisms/BrandPortfolio`): `Default` (all collapsed), `SonicSelected`, `EchoParkSelected` (demonstrates the `#cta-echopark` slot for primary + secondary CTAs), `TacticalFleetSelected` (description-only body), `PowersportsSelected`, `Interactive`
- **Storybook `title`**: `Organisms/BrandPortfolio`

## Compare Tool

### `CompareTool` — `src/components/CompareTool/`
- **Figma**: no dedicated frame — designed against existing EPDS modal / grid / tile conventions.
- **Role**: SRP compare modal. Overlays the SRP without unmounting it so every piece of SRP state (scroll position, filter selections, active pills, `compared` flags) is preserved when closed.
- **Props**: `modelValue: boolean` (**required**, v-model), `vehicles: CompareVehicle[]` (**required**), `title?: string` (default `'Compare vehicles'`), `isSonic?: boolean` (forwards `vehicleStatus` to inner tiles when `true`), `emptyLabel?: string`
- **Type export**: `CompareVehicle` — superset of the `SrpTile` props (`id, year, mileage, stockNumber, title, price, monthlyPayment, deliveryLabel/Store/Distance, vehicleStatus, imageUrl, imageCount, favorited, href`) plus comparison-only fields (`trim, bodyStyle, engine, transmission, driveType, mpgCity, mpgHwy, exteriorColor, interiorColor, features`)
- **Emits**:
  - `update:modelValue: [boolean]`
  - `update:favorited: [{ id, value: boolean }]` — mirrors `SrpTile`'s favorite toggle scoped by vehicle id
  - `remove: [{ id }]` — X icon on a tile clicked
- **Composes**: `Overlay` (scrim + teleport + Esc + scroll-lock + click-to-dismiss at `zIndex: 1000`), `SrpTile` (one per column — used unchanged), `SmallIconButton` (X overlay on each tile + close icon), `MediumIconButton` (header close)
- **Layout**:
  - Centered panel: `width: min(1280px, 95vw)`, `max-height: 88vh`, `border-radius: --border-radius-lg`, `box-shadow: --shadow-level-3`
  - Header: title (`--text-h4-*`) + close `MediumIconButton`, separated by `--border-width-hairline` divider
  - Body: vertically + horizontally scrollable, holds two stacked siblings (`tile-bar` + `compare-grid`) that share the same `--label-col-w / --vehicle-col-w` custom properties so columns align.
  - **Sticky tile bar** (`.compare-tool__tile-bar`): a single block element with `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 5`, a solid `--color-neutral-100` background and `--border-width-hairline` bottom border. `width: max-content; min-width: 100%` keeps the bar **at least** as wide as the visible body (so no whitespace to the left or right of the tiles) while growing to content max-content when there are more vehicles than fit. Inside, a nested CSS grid renders the empty label column + one `SrpTile` per vehicle.
  - **Comparison grid** (`.compare-tool__compare-grid`): same column template as the tile-grid, `width: max-content; min-width: 100%`. Section headings (`grid-column: 1 / -1`) and row labels are `position: sticky; left: var(--spacing-xxs)` to anchor visibly during horizontal scroll without drifting under the grid's left padding.
  - **X (remove) overlay**: 32×32 `SmallIconButton` absolutely positioned at `top: 16px; left: 16px` on each tile (mirrors the favorite at top-right). `z-index: 6` to clear `SrpTile`'s internal stacking.
- **Comparison rows** (deduped — anything `SrpTile` already shows is intentionally excluded):
  - **Basics**: Trim, Body style
  - **Drivetrain & efficiency**: Engine, Transmission, Drive type, MPG (city / hwy)
  - **Color**: Exterior color, Interior color
  - **Features**: comma-separated feature list
  - Missing values render as `'—'`. Section headings span the full grid (`grid-column: 1 / -1`) at `--text-h6-bold-*`.
- **Responsive**:
  - **Tablet (≤1023.98px)**: `--label-col-w: 140px`, `--vehicle-col-w: 280px` (matches `SrpTile`'s natural `min-width` so the tile never overflows its grid cell). Tiles past what fits live behind a horizontal swipe.
  - **Mobile (<600px)**: **full-screen overlay** — panel is `width: 100vw`, `height: 100dvh` (with `100vh` fallback), `border-radius: 0`, no box-shadow, and the `Overlay` scrim padding collapses to 0. `--label-col-w: 96px`, `--vehicle-col-w: 280px` — same 280px floor as tablet so tiles render at their designed minimum. Horizontal swipe walks through vehicles.
- **Auto-close**: if `vehicles.length` drops to `0` while the modal is open (every tile removed via the X), the component emits `update:modelValue: false` so the user lands back on the SRP cleanly.
- **State preservation**: the modal is a teleport overlay — `SrpPage` never unmounts. Closing via the header X, Esc, or backdrop click drops the overlay only; SRP scroll, filter selections, pill bar, and compare flags survive untouched.
- **Brand awareness**: brand-agnostic — `SrpTile` already swaps brand-coloured pieces (price, primary action) automatically via tokens. `isSonic` is purely a passthrough for the `vehicleStatus` row on tiles.
- **Accessibility**: `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal="true"`, `aria-label` from `title`. Tile X buttons get a per-vehicle `aria-label` (`Remove <title> from compare`).
- **SrpPage integration**: opens when the user clicks `Compare` on `CompareTray`; the page maps `listings.filter(c => c.compared)` to the `CompareTool`'s `vehicles` prop. `@remove` writes `car.compared = false`; `@update:favorited` mirrors back into the source listing so the SRP tile reflects the change after close.
- **Stories** (`Organisms/CompareTool`): `TwoVehicles`, `ThreeVehicles`, `FourVehicles`, `SonicVehicleStatus`, `Mobile`, `Interactive`
- **Storybook `title`**: `Organisms/CompareTool`

