## Pages (`src/pages/`)

Full-page compositions — not published library components, used for Storybook page-level demos.

### `SrpPage` — `src/pages/SrpPage.vue`
- **Role**: Full SRP (Search Results Page) composition
- **Props**: `brandName?: string` (default `'EchoPark'`), `phoneNumber?: string` (default `'(877) 708-4049'`)
- **Brand awareness**: An internal `isSonic` computed (derived from `brandName`) drives brand-specific overrides for `GlobalFooter` and **swaps the entire header**: Sonic renders the new `SonicNavBar` organism (mega-menu + mobile drawer, `:sticky="false"` so it doesn't fight the SRP's own sticky filter sidebar) while EchoPark continues to use the legacy `GlobalHeader` (`variant="global-search"` with zip / phone). The Sonic primary-nav structure is sourced from the shared `src/pages/sonicNavItems.ts`.
- **Composes**: `SonicNavBar` (Sonic) **or** `GlobalHeader` (EchoPark), `GlobalFooter`, `SrpTile`, `CompareTray`, `CompareTool`, `Pagination`, `SeoCarousel`, `SrpFiltersPanel`, all SRP filter components (Vehicle status + Condition are both Sonic-only; EchoPark shows 10, Sonic shows 12 with Vehicle status directly above Condition at the top of the list after Distance), `SrpFilterPill`, `BaseButton`
- **Vehicle-status filtering**: `SrpPage` seeds each listing with an optional `vehicleStatus` and derives `visibleListings = listings.filter(...)` that honours the Vehicle-status filter selections. Tiles in the grid iterate over `visibleListings`, and `toggleFavorite` / `toggleCompared` now key off `car.id` (not array index) so filtered views still write back to the right listing. The `vehicleStatus` prop is only passed to tiles when `isSonic` — EchoPark tiles always render the delivery block.
- **Compare flow**: each `VehicleListing` is extended with comparison-only fields (`trim, bodyStyle, engine, transmission, driveType, mpgCity, mpgHwy, exteriorColor, interiorColor, features`) seeded from a per-slot `COMPARISON_SEEDS` table so the modal columns differ. `comparedVehicles` is a computed mapping of `listings.filter(c => c.compared)` to `CompareVehicle`. `showCompareTool` ref opens the `CompareTool` overlay from the tray's `@compare`; the tray's `@cancel` event walks `listings` and zeros every `compared` flag (the tray auto-hides when count returns to 0). The `CompareTool`'s `@remove` and `@update:favorited` events write back to the source listing so the SRP tiles reflect any in-modal changes after close. Because `SrpPage` itself never unmounts while the overlay is open, scroll / filter / pill / compare state is preserved across open → close.
- **Stories** (`Pages/SRP`): `EchoPark Brand` (default brand + globals) and `Sonic Automotive Brand` (passes `brandName: 'Sonic Automotive'` + Sonic globals for primitives toggle)
- **Storybook `title`**: `Pages/SRP`

### `VdpPage` — `src/pages/VdpPage.vue`
- **Role**: Vehicle Detail Page composition. First pass is **desktop + Sonic-only + above-the-fold only**; below-the-fold sections are flagged in-file with a `TODO`.
- **Props**: `brandName?: string` (default `'Sonic Automotive'`), `phoneNumber?: string` (default `'(877) 708-4049'`)
- **Composes**: `SonicNavBar` (Sonic) **or** `GlobalHeader` (EchoPark), `GlobalFooter`, `VdpGallery`, `VdpSummary`. Hero row is a flex container with `gap: 80px` (Figma spec) that shrinks to `--spacing-xxl` below 1280 px.
- **Seed data**: Matches the Figma frame — 2026 BMW X5 M60i, `$50,000` MSRP, `BMW of Birmingham`, VIN `5UX33EU01T9307218`, Stock `T9307218`. `favorited` is a local `ref(false)` toggled via `@update:favorited` on `VdpGallery`. `onTestDrive`, `onSeeStorePrice`, and `onOpenPhotos` are stubbed to `console.log`.
- **Brand awareness**: Same white-label pattern as `SrpPage`: `isSonic` swaps the header (`SonicNavBar` for Sonic, sticky enabled here because the VDP doesn't have its own top-of-viewport sticky element; `GlobalHeader` for EchoPark) and overrides the footer logo / link columns / legal / social / copyright. Sonic primary-nav structure imported from the shared `src/pages/sonicNavItems.ts`. Today only the Sonic brand variant is published as a Storybook page demo.
- **Stories** (`Pages/VDP`): `Sonic Automotive Brand` with `layout: 'fullscreen'`.
- **Storybook `title`**: `Pages/VDP`
